--- build/config docs ---
(ocamltest and converting C compiler warnings to errors).

2. Consult link:INSTALL.adoc[] for build instructions. Here is the gist of it:
+
----
./configure
make -j 4
----
If you are on a release build and need development options, you can add
`--enable-ocamltest` (to allow running the testsuite) and `--enable-warn-error`
(so you don't get caught by CI later!).

3. Try the newly built compiler binaries `ocamlc`, `ocamlopt` or their
`.opt` version. To try the toplevel, use:
+
37-
38-* If you do not have write access to `/tmp`, you should set the environment
39-  variable `TMPDIR` to the name of some other temporary directory.
40-
41-* The zstd library is used for compression of marshaled data. The option
42:  `--without-zstd` may be passed to `configure` in order to disable it.
43-
44-== Prerequisites (special cases)
45-
46-* Under Cygwin, the `gcc-core` package is required. `flexdll` is also necessary
47-  for shared library support.
48-
49-* Binutils including `ar` and `strip` are required if your distribution
50-  does not already provide them with the C compiler.
51-
52-== Configuration
53-
54-From the top directory, do:
55-
56:        ./configure
57-
58-This generates the three configuration files `Makefile.config`,
59-`runtime/caml/m.h` and `runtime/caml/s.h`.
60-
61:The `configure` script accepts options that can be discovered by running:
62-
63:        ./configure --help
64-
65-Some options or variables like LDLIBS may not be taken into account
66-by the OCaml build system at the moment. Please report an issue if you
67-discover such a variable or option and this causes troubles to you.
68-
69-Examples:
70-
71-* Standard installation in `/usr/{bin,lib,man}` instead of `/usr/local`:
72:    ./configure --prefix=/usr
73-
74-
75-* On a Linux x86-64 host, to build a 32-bit version of OCaml:
76-
77:    ./configure --build=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu --host=i686-linux-gnu
78-
79-* For AIX 7.x with the IBM compiler `xlc`:
80-
81:    ./configure CC=xlc
82-+
83-By default, build is 32-bit. For 64-bit build, please set environment variable `OBJECT_MODE=64`
84:  for _both_ `configure` and `make world` phases. Note, if this variable is set for only one phase,
85-  your build will break (`ocamlrun` segfaults).
86-+
87-* For Solaris/Illumos on SPARC machines with Sun PRO compiler only 64-bit
88-  bytecode target is supported (32-bit fails due to alignment issues; the optimization
89-  is preset to `-O4` for inlining):
90-
91:    ./configure CC="cc -m64"
92-+
93-If something goes wrong during the automatic configuration, or if the generated
94-files cause errors later on, then look at the template files:
95-
96-        Makefile.config.in
97-        Makefile.build_config.in
98-        runtime/caml/m.h.in
99-        runtime/caml/s.h.in
100-+
101-for guidance on how to edit the generated files by hand.
102-
103-== Building the compiler
104-
105-From the top directory, do:
106-
107-        make
108-
109-This builds the OCaml compiler for the first time.  This phase is
110-fairly verbose; consider redirecting the output to a file:
111-
112-        make > make.log 2>&1     # in sh
113-        make >& make.log         # in csh
114-
115-== (Optional) Running the testsuite
